{
    "test_name": "MOB.512_AssetVerify_Job_List_Status",
    "details": {
        "name": "MOB.512_AssetVerify_Job_List_Status",
        "type": "browser",
        "status": "paused",
        "message": "`MOB.512` The job **list** reflects a completed job.\n- Verifies both assets on the detail page, returns to the list, and asserts what the LIST   renders: the card's own `2 out of 2 Assets Verified` with `100%`, and that the `Completed` badge keeps   the job while `Ready` hides it \u2014 the inverse of `MOB.560`'s resting shape.\n- The status dot is a colour, not text, so the badge filter is what can read the status   back from the list at all.\n- **SELF-RESTORING**: returns to the job and unverifies both on `always` legs, which   recomputes it to `READY`.\n- \ud83d\uded1 Must run LAST in `MOB.963` alongside `MOB.511`: mid-flight the fixture is `2 out of 2 Assets Verified`.",
        "tags": [
            "Mobile",
            "env:dev",
            "Asset Verification",
            "CRUD",
            "self-restoring"
        ],
        "locations": [
            "gcp:us-west2"
        ],
        "config": {
            "assertions": [],
            "config_variables": [
                {
                    "id": "fe7958bf-435f-4932-af8e-0931caab79e7",
                    "name": "MOBDEV",
                    "type": "global"
                }
            ],
            "request": {
                "headers": {},
                "method": "GET",
                "url": "{{ MOBDEV }}"
            },
            "variables": [
                {
                    "id": "fe7958bf-435f-4932-af8e-0931caab79e7",
                    "name": "MOBDEV",
                    "type": "global"
